:INFO
Art. 19 Evaluation
1 The FDPIC shall review the execution and effectiveness of this Act and, in particular, the costs incurred in its implementation, and shall report on a regular basis to the Federal Council.
2 The FDPIC shall submit the first report on the costs of implementing this Act to the Federal Council within three years of it coming into force.
3 The FDPIC’s reports shall be published.
|

:INFO
Art. 20 Right to information and inspection
1 Within the context of mediation proceedings, the FDPIC shall have access to official documents, even if they are subject to secrecy.
2 The FDPIC shall be subject to official secrecy to the same extent as the authorities whose official documents he or she inspects or from whom he or she obtains information.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Amended by Annex 1 No II 10 of the Data Protection Act of 25 Sept. 2020, in force since 1 Sept. 2023 (AS 2022 491; BBl 2017 6941).

